From be76946f5a243223e0d43d431bae14291d7d5e1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maximiliano <m.lopz.montn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:02:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: retro guestbook.exe backed by Vercel Redis
 (KV_REDIS_URL)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New api/guestbook route (GET/POST) using a real Redis TCP client
(node-redis) against KV_REDIS_URL — Vercel's current Redis product only
provides a redis:// connection string, not the older Upstash REST API.
Connection is cached across warm serverless invocations. Falls back to
a clean 'not configured' response when the env var isn't set, instead
of crashing the route.

New Guestbook.tsx window matching the existing win98 styling, wired
into the desktop icons and the terminal ('guestbook' / 'sign' commands).
Basic spam guard: honeypot field, name/message length caps. Entry text
renders through React (no dangerouslySetInnerHTML), so it's inert even
if someone submits HTML/script in a message.

Verified end-to-end against a local Redis instance: empty GET, POST
persists and round-trips, honeypot silently drops spam, and the whole
route degrades cleanly to 'not configured' with KV_REDIS_URL unset.
